SUMMARY:Showing of ‘Nuevo Mundo’
LOCATION:Bartram’s Garden Barn
DESCRIPTION:Join us for this screening of the film Nuevo Mundo (1978\, unr
 ated\, duration: 1 hour\, 35 minutes)\, which tells the story of a priest 
 in 16th-century Mexico who converts the local population to Christianity b
 y making a statue of the Virgin Mary in the image of local indigenous wome
 n. This screening will be followed by an open discussion. While you’re h
 ere\, be sure to check out the Meeting of the Condor and the Eagle Indigen
 ous art exhibition. Open gallery hours are from 12–4pm.\n\nListing: http
 s://www.bartramsgarden.org/event/showing-of-nuevo-mundo/
URL:https://www.bartramsgarden.org/event/showing-of-nuevo-mundo/
CATEGORIES:Arts & Performance,Free Community Events
END:VEVENT
